  "goodToKnow": "Das Kaiserreich is an empire, and in German history it usually means das Deutsche Kaiserreich (1871–1918), founded under Prussian leadership when Wilhelm I was proclaimed Kaiser in the Hall of Mirrors at Versailles. It ended when Wilhelm II abdicated in November 1918. Der Kaiser comes from Caesar. A Kaisersemmel is an Austrian bread roll. Plural: die Kaiserreiche."
